    "plotType": "Multi-line plot of SPL (dB) vs. log frequency, one curve per loudness level",
    "description": "Equal-loudness contours map, for each frequency, the sound pressure level needed to make a tone sound equally loud to a listener. Each curve is one loudness level in phons (anchored to its dB SPL value at 1 kHz), and the family traces how human hearing sensitivity varies with pitch. The characteristic U-shape shows we hear midrange best and need far more level at the low and very high extremes.",
