    "whatItTellsYou": "The height of a contour at a given frequency is how many dB SPL that pitch needs to match the loudness of a 1 kHz tone, so the deep dip around 3-4 kHz reveals where the ear is most sensitive (the ear-canal resonance). The steep rise at low frequencies shows bass must be much louder in dB to be heard as loud, and the flattening of the curves at high phon levels shows loud sounds are perceived more uniformly across frequency than quiet ones.",
