    "whatItTellsYou": "The number of amplitude swells per second is the beat frequency, which equals the difference between the two tone frequencies, so counting beats tells you exactly how far apart the pitches are. Slow, widely spaced beats mean the tones are almost in tune, while fast beats mean a larger mistuning; the beats vanishing to a steady amplitude is the moment the two frequencies match.",
